  "extractionNotes": "Self-employed mother (standard contributions, voluntary sickness insurance from 2023-08-18) with twins born 2025-01-15. Long sickness in pregnancy on a chain of e-ZLA certificates, each followed by a Z-3b she filed herself; typed ZUS note: sickness benefit paid 2024-09-27..2025-01-08 and maternity benefit 2025-01-09..2026-04-08 (455 days = 31 weeks of maternity for twins + 34 weeks of parental). Maternity started 6 days before the birth, directly after the sickness. ZAM: maternity from 2025-01-09 (end written as 2025-08-18, inconsistent with the parental start 2025-08-14; the 31-week end 2025-08-13 is used) and parental 2025-08-14..2026-04-08; 81.5% box unticked, joint claim, 81.5% inferred. Father's statement of non-use over the mother's parental period. Two ZUS insurance memos (study dates 2024-09-27 and 2025-01-09): no arrears on either date; declared bases 4161.00 (2023-09..12) and 4694.40 (2024-01..09); two short earlier employee titles in 2023-09 and 2023-10 ended by deregistration (not modelled). Sick-note letter code not legible; pregnancy code B inferred. Rates not printed. Address and bank-account change letters omitted."
